; HAVARTH.SCR — The New Havarth Mining Company: "The Surveyor's Commission"
; =============================================================================
; Four surveying assignments for the New Havarth Mining Company in Fayd's North
; Bazaar, each unlocked by finishing the one before. No GM is needed: the
; Havarths are room messages, not NPCs, and every step is scripted.
;
;   1. The Inner Sea caves        3 readings   100 gold crowns    1,000 XP
;   2. The Abandoned Dig          4 readings   250 gold crowns    2,000 XP
;   3. Beneath the Matriarch      3 readings   500 gold crowns    4,000 XP
;   4. The Teeth of Shartan       5 readings 1,000 gold crowns    8,000 XP
;                                            + Havarth Masterwork Mining Axe
;
; Needs HAVARTHITEMS.SCR (the instrument and the axe) loaded first.
; See original/HAVARTH_RUNBOOK.md for the walkthrough and GM fix-ups.
;
; Per character (INTNUM, persistent):
;   1040  stage: 0 none, 1/3/5/7 assignment 1-4 under way, 2/4/6 assignment
;         1-3 paid, 8 all four done (axe given)
;   1041-1045  readings taken this assignment (1 = taken), one per survey spot
;   1046  1 = Mara has compiled this assignment's report for Edric
;   1049  scratch: 1 = the reading just taken finished the assignment
; One-time experience: AWARD 1040-1043.
;
; ID ranges (the 94xx block is reserved for the New Havarth quests):
;   NUMBER 9400-9402 (company offices), 9410-9413 (the Shartan prospect)
;   MACRO 9400-9407   CEVENT 9400
; Overrides: room 394 (adds the staircase up, Bram, and his lines) and the
; newsboard, item 304 (adds a "Surveyors Wanted" page).
; =============================================================================

; ── The company building ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

; Room 394, copied from FAYDINDR.SCR. Changes: Bram Havarth at the counter, a
; staircase up to the offices (EXIT U 9400), and his IFSAY lines.
NUMBER 394
NAME New Havarth Mining Company
DEEPCAVE
FIXED_LIGHT
CALL 33
*DESCRIPTION_START
The wooden floor creaks under the strain of miners carrying their heavy ore. From behind a counter, Bram Havarth, the company's grizzled treasurer, weighs each load over the top of his rather dusty spectacles, counts out the coins with visible reluctance, and notes everything in a small brown book. With their newly earned wealth, miners can purchase the provisions on sale here. A sign details the prices. There is a door here with something written on it, and a sturdy staircase climbs to the company offices above.
*DESCRIPTION_END
TRAINING 35 30
EXIT O 207
EXIT U 9400
BUY_ORE
ITEM 0 204 ADJ1=355
ITEM 1 852
ITEM 2 1432 ADJ1=288 ADJ2=192
ITEM 3 943 VAL2=395 UNLOCKED
ITEM 9 693 ADJ1=10

IFENTRY
	IFVAR NIGHT = 1
		IFITEM 3 OPEN
			CLOSE 3
			AFFECT 395
			CLOSE 1
			ECHO ALL The clerk speaks up brightly, " Closing time! Everybody out!"
			MOVEALL 394
			AFFECT 394
			ECHO ALL Everyone in the claims office suddenly arrives, and the door slams shut behind them.
		ENDIF
	ENDIF
ENDIF
IFPREVERB OPEN 3
	IFVAR NIGHT = 1
		ECHO ALL You hear a voice from behind the door, "Go away, we're closed."
		CLEARVERB
	ENDIF
ENDIF
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM READ 3
   Royal Land Office
    Claims Division
*DESCRIPTION_END
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM EXAM 2
The shiny metal scale has a large platform on the top for placing bulky items. The weight of the items depresses a spring that moves an arrow to a number corresponding with the weight. After making sure only the item you want to weigh is on the scale, you can take a reading.
*DESCRIPTION_END
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM ON 1
You see a working scale.
*DESCRIPTION_END
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM READ 0
Item             Price
----             -----
Lantern        20 crowns
Torch           1 crown
Sack            4 crowns
Backpack        5 crowns
Sheath          2 crowns
Pick-axe       20 crowns
Shovel         20 crowns
Miner's Hammer 10 crowns
*DESCRIPTION_END
STOREITEM 89 -1 2000
STOREITEM 466 -1 100
STOREITEM 95 -1 400
STOREITEM 491 -1 500
STOREITEM 467 -1 200
STOREITEM 1506 -1 2000
STOREITEM 484 -1 2000
STOREITEM 766 796 10
IFSAY WORK
  IFVAR DUMMY8 = 0
    EQUAL DUMMY8 1
    CALL 9405
  ENDIF
ENDIF
IFSAY JOB
  IFVAR DUMMY8 = 0
    EQUAL DUMMY8 1
    CALL 9405
  ENDIF
ENDIF
IFSAY SURVEY
  IFVAR DUMMY8 = 0
    EQUAL DUMMY8 1
    CALL 9405
  ENDIF
ENDIF
IFSAY EDRIC
  IFVAR DUMMY8 = 0
    EQUAL DUMMY8 1
    CALL 9405
  ENDIF
ENDIF
;
NUMBER 9400
NAME New Havarth Mining Company, main office
DEEPCAVE
FIXED_LIGHT
CALL 33
*DESCRIPTION_START
Large maps of the lands surrounding Fayd cover the walls of this busy office, and tables hold mineral samples, surveying instruments and stacks of carefully organized documents. Behind a broad oak desk, Master Edric Havarth, a shrewd highlander in his late forties, looks up from a ledger with the air of a man who expects good news. A heavy ironbound strongbox squats in the corner. The sound of hammering drifts in from the scaffolding outside. Doorways lead west to the surveying room and east to the workshop, and a staircase goes down to the counter.
*DESCRIPTION_END
EXIT D 394
EXIT W 9401
EXIT E 9402
ITEM 0 1060
ITEM 1 69 ADJ1=216
ITEM 2 228 ADJ1=9311
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM EXAM 0
The largest map shows Fayd at its center, with the Inner Sea to the south, the Grymwood to the west and the jagged Teeth of Shartan to the north. Pins with little paper flags mark the caves beneath the Inner Sea, an old dig east of the city, and the Matriarch Tree. A great many pins have been stuck into the mountains, pulled out again, and stuck in somewhere else.
*DESCRIPTION_END
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM EXAM 1
The broad oak desk is buried in ledgers, contracts and letters. A neatly lettered card propped against the inkwell reads: "A pickaxe earns a day's wage. Knowing where to swing it earns a fortune."
*DESCRIPTION_END
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM EXAM 2
The heavy ironbound strongbox is secured with three locks. Edric keeps the keys on a chain around his neck.
*DESCRIPTION_END
IFENTRY
  IFVAR INTNUM1040 = 0
    ECHO PLAYER Edric Havarth sets down his pen. "Looking for work? Say so, then. I've no time for guessing games."
  ENDIF
  IFVAR INTNUM1040 = 2
    ECHO PLAYER Edric Havarth beckons you over. "There you are! I've another assignment, if you're ready for work."
  ENDIF
  IFVAR INTNUM1040 = 4
    ECHO PLAYER Edric Havarth beckons you over. "There you are! I've another assignment, if you're ready for work."
  ENDIF
  IFVAR INTNUM1040 = 6
    ECHO PLAYER Edric Havarth rises from his chair. "Ah. I've been hoping you'd come by. Tell me you're ready for work."
  ENDIF
  IFVAR INTNUM1046 = 1
    ECHO PLAYER Edric Havarth has your survey report spread open on his desk. "Mara's sent your report through. Shall we settle up? Tell me about your survey."
  ENDIF
ENDIF
IFSAY WORK
  IFVAR DUMMY8 = 0
    EQUAL DUMMY8 1
    CALL 9401
  ENDIF
ENDIF
IFSAY JOB
  IFVAR DUMMY8 = 0
    EQUAL DUMMY8 1
    CALL 9401
  ENDIF
ENDIF
IFSAY ASSIGNMENT
  IFVAR DUMMY8 = 0
    EQUAL DUMMY8 1
    CALL 9401
  ENDIF
ENDIF
IFSAY SURVEY
  IFVAR DUMMY8 = 0
    EQUAL DUMMY8 1
    CALL 9401
  ENDIF
ENDIF
IFSAY REPORT
