NUMBER 9401
NAME New Havarth Mining Company, surveying room
DEEPCAVE
FIXED_LIGHT
CALL 33
*DESCRIPTION_START
A broad wooden desk is covered with geological charts, brass instruments and trays of labeled stone samples, and several partially completed survey reports await examination. Mara Havarth, the company's chief surveyor, bends over a chart with a magnifying lens, muttering figures under her breath. She is practical, meticulous, and visibly impatient with anyone who wastes her time. A small sign is propped on the corner of the desk. A doorway leads east to the main office.
*DESCRIPTION_END
EXIT E 9400
ITEM 0 69 ADJ1=355
ITEM 1 187
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM EXAM 0
Charts, rock samples in labeled trays, and a half-finished brass instrument with its dials taken apart cover every inch of the desk.
*DESCRIPTION_END
