NUMBER 9402
NAME New Havarth Mining Company, workshop
DEEPCAVE
FIXED_LIGHT
CALL 33
*DESCRIPTION_START
The smell of oil and worked metal fills this crowded workshop. Picks, hammers and other mining tools hang neatly from racks beside a sturdy workbench, where Tessa Havarth, Edric's daughter, frowns at the edge of a battered pickaxe and reaches for a whetstone. A doorway leads west to the main office.
*DESCRIPTION_END
EXIT W 9400
ITEM 0 471
ITEM 1 225 ADJ1=1225
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM EXAM 0
Pickaxes, shovels, hammers and pry bars hang in neat rows, each tagged with a scrap of paper naming the miner who signed it out and the day it is due back.
*DESCRIPTION_END
*DESCRIPTION_START ITEM EXAM 1
The workbench is scarred from years of use. A vise holds a pickaxe head, and a row of files and whetstones is laid out in order of coarseness.
*DESCRIPTION_END
